# Movies — American pictures from 1930 to 1955 whose US copyright was not
# renewed, long distributed as public domain and held in the Internet
# Archive's curated feature_films collection. Brazil: 70 years from
# publication, Law 9.610/98 art. 44, so 1955 is the limit in 2026.
# Foreign productions are deliberately absent: the URAA restored US
# copyright in foreign works in 1996, so a lapsed renewal does not make
# them free there — that excluded the British Hitchcocks, Korda's Jungle
# Book and others. Also absent: studio pictures with no documented
# non-renewal, exploitation films, atrocity footage, and the Tarzan
# pictures, which are public domain as films while the name is a
# trademark the Burroughs estate enforces.
